# MCP RFC 9728 + RFC 8707 conformance

This rule scopes AGENTS hard rule 49 + the Workstream E additions
from the Data Layer Selective Additive Enhancement.

## What changed

- [`aqp/api/well_known.py`](mdc:aqp/api/well_known.py) publishes
  OAuth 2.0 Protected Resource Metadata (RFC 9728) at the root and
  per-MCP-server paths.
- [`aqp/api/mcp_audience.py`](mdc:aqp/api/mcp_audience.py) validates
  the `aud` / `resource` claim of every access token reaching the
  MCP servers (RFC 8707 Resource Indicators).
- Both [`aqp-data-mcp`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/server.py) and
  [`aqp-codebase-mcp`](mdc:aqp/codebase/mcp/server.py) call
  :func:`validate_mcp_audience` on every `tools/call`.
- The [`tests/mcp/test_no_token_passthrough.py`](mdc:tests/mcp/test_no_token_passthrough.py)
  linter scans the MCP packages for any code path that would
  forward an incoming user Bearer token to an upstream API — the
  2025-11-25 MCP spec explicitly forbids this.

## Hard rules

1. **Per-server canonical URI.** Each MCP server MUST advertise its
   canonical URI via `settings.mcp_data_canonical_uri` /
   `settings.mcp_codebase_canonical_uri`. Production deployments set
   both explicitly so the audience-bound tokens minted by the AS
   match what the server advertises.
2. **PKCE S256 only.** No plaintext / no other challenge methods.
   The :class:`IdentityProvider.login_url` ABC now accepts an
   RFC 8707 ``resource`` kwarg; MCP clients MUST pass it on both
   authorize and token requests.
3. **No token passthrough.** When the MCP server calls upstream
   APIs on the user's behalf, it MUST mint its own M2M token via
   :class:`M2MTokenIssuer`. Direct
   `request.headers["Authorization"]` forwarding into outbound
   `httpx` calls is forbidden — the
   [`test_no_token_passthrough`](mdc:tests/mcp/test_no_token_passthrough.py)
   linter enforces this at CI time.
4. **WWW-Authenticate header on 401.** Audience-mismatch 401s MUST
   carry the RFC 9728 `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
   resource_metadata="…"` header so MCP clients can bootstrap
   discovery. The
   [`build_resource_metadata_header`](mdc:aqp/api/mcp_audience.py)
   helper builds this for you; don't hand-roll the value.
5. **Rollout modes.** `AQP_MCP_REQUIRE_RFC8707` accepts
   `off` (rollout default), `permissive` (log + OTel tag without
   rejecting), `strict` (raise 401 with WWW-Authenticate header).
   Flip strict only after 24 h of zero would-be denies in
   permissive mode.

## Reference CVEs (why this matters)

- **CVE-2025-49596** (Anthropic MCP Inspector, CVSS 9.4) —
  unauthenticated RCE; demonstrated the impact of skipping
  audience binding on MCP-adjacent surfaces.
- **CVE-2025-6514** (`mcp-remote`, CVSS 9.6) — OS command injection
  via a malicious MCP server; another consequence of weak token
  scoping.

## Don't

- Don't add new MCP servers without publishing a matching
  `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/...` document.
- Don't relax PKCE to `plain` for compatibility with a buggy AS.
  Replace the AS instead.
- Don't accept a `resource` parameter from the request body — only
  from the authorize URL / token endpoint per RFC 8707.
- Don't read `audience` from the request body for MCP routes; the
  validator reads it from the verified JWT
  (`request.state.oidc_claims`) only.
